{
 "_comment": [
  "UNVERIFIED: written from documented output, not run against a device. Junos prints `| display json` as text, so each value here is the reply's lines. Rows come from several documented examples, not from one device.",
  "show chassis hardware | display json: https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/software/junos/junos-xml-protocol/topics/task/junos-xml-protocol-command-output-mapping-to-json.html (the whole non-compact example; its `additional JSON objects` placeholder is removed). It has no transceiver; the Xcvr path is covered in test_ports_parse.py.",
  "show interfaces terse | display json: not printed by Juniper. Juniper documents the XML (https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/software/junos/automation-scripting/topics/example/junos-script-automation-op-script-customizing-output.html: physical-interface, logical-interface, name, admin-status, oper-status, address-family/address-family-name) and the rule that maps XML to this JSON (https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/software/junos/junos-xml-protocol/topics/task/junos-xml-protocol-command-output-mapping-to-json.html). The rows and addresses are copied from the `show interfaces terse` examples in https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/software/junos/interfaces-fundamentals/topics/ref/command/show-interfaces-terse.html and https://www.juniper.net/documentation/us/en/software/junos/interfaces-ethernet/topics/ref/command/show-interfaces-terse.html; the JSON is that rule applied to them. `interface-address/ifa-local` is the Junos XML API's name for the Local column and is not in a page I could read.",
  "show interfaces descriptions | display json: not printed by Juniper either; the same rule applied to the rows of the `show interfaces descriptions` example (juniper.net/documentation/en_US/junos13.1/topics/reference/command-summary/show-interfaces-descriptions.html) with the `description` element the op-script page names.",
  "show lldp neighbors | display json: the same rule applied to rows of the EX Series `show lldp neighbors` example (juniper.net/documentation/en_US/junos13.2/topics/reference/command-summary/show-lldp-neighbors-lldp-ex-series.html); element names are those of Juniper's PyEZ op table, jnpr/junos/op/lldp.yml."
 ],
